<header class="page-hero page-hero-split">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">Approach</p><h1>We work from the argument outward<span class="red-stop">.</span></h1></div>
  <p class="page-lede">Good visual communication begins before layout. We work with your subject experts to clarify what the audience needs to understand, then find the clearest way to communicate it.</p>
</header>

<section class="approach-steps">
  <article class="approach-step fade-in"><span>01</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Understand</p><h2>Purpose, audience and evidence</h2><p>We begin with what the communication must do, who it is for and what the source material can support. We can start with notes, drafts, data, interviews or existing documents.</p></div><aside>What must change for the audience after they have seen this?</aside></article>
  <article class="approach-step fade-in"><span>02</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Structure</p><h2>Argument, hierarchy and sequence</h2><p>We interrogate the material, identify what matters most and shape a clear order. This may mean finding the argument, simplifying the flow or separating different levels of detail.</p></div><aside>What is the one idea the whole structure must make easier to see?</aside></article>
  <article class="approach-step fade-in"><span>03</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Explain</p><h2>Charts, diagrams and visual form</h2><p>We choose visual forms because of the job they do: showing magnitude, change, cause, sequence, comparison, risk or a decision. The site examples include charts, maps, timelines, systems diagrams and bespoke graphics.</p></div><aside>Which relationship cannot be understood quickly enough in prose alone?</aside></article>
  <article class="approach-step fade-in"><span>04</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Deliver</p><h2>Polished, editable and usable outputs</h2><p>We build the final resource for its real context: live presentation, asynchronous reading, board review, publication or digital use. Review stages, quality assurance and practical handover are part of the work.</p></div><aside>Will the output still work when the team needs to use and update it?</aside></article>
</section>

